From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 02:11:12 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 09/60] input: mouse, touch and soft-keyboard calls reach the
 session in call order

session_send_mouse, session_send_pointer, session_input_key and
session_input_string were normal flutter_rust_bridge calls, which run on its
4-thread pool. Calls Dart makes back to back (a burst of pointer moves after
the UI thread was busy, the Backspaces and the text of one soft-keyboard
edit) then raced each other into the session channel and could arrive out of
order: the cursor jumped back to an older position, a soft-keyboard edit
typed its text before deleting.

They now return SyncReturn, like session_enter_or_leave, and run on the
calling Dart thread in order. The Rust side only parses the event and puts a
message on the session channel. The awaits on the mouse calls go, since a
void result cannot be awaited; the web bridge returns void as well.

The hardware-keyboard calls (session_handle_flutter_key_event and its raw
variant) stay as they are: no reported problem goes through them, and they
serve desktop input source 2 and hardware keyboards on phones and tablets.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
